src/backend/access/yb_scan/README

YB Scan Layer
=============

This directory implements scans of YB relations: the tableam scan callbacks
for YB tables and the accessors that executor nodes still call on them, the
scan primitives that the YB index access methods (yb_lsm, ybgin, and ybvector)
share, the plan-time scan logic that the planner shares, the YB implementation
of genam's systable scans, ANALYZE row sampling, and single-row fetch by
ybctid.  The headers that the groups below list are all under
src/include/access/.  Most of them are implemented in this directory, but four
are implemented in src/backend/access/common/: yb_cost.h, yb_target.h,
yb_lockrows.h, and yb_parallel_scan.h.  #37429 and #37428 track moving the
implementations of all but yb_target.h to directories that match their roles.

Code above the access-method layer, such as executor nodes, the optimizer,
commands, and catalog and cache code, should reach YB relations only through
the interfaces upstream code uses for any table or index access method:
tableam, the index AM interface, and genam's systable functions.  YB extends
those interfaces where it needs to, as with table_beginscan_*_yb() and the
yb_ammightrecheck index AM callback, rather than going around them.  The write
path, which goes around tuple_insert, tuple_update, and tuple_delete, is not
structured this way yet, but new write-path code should still go through
tableam where it can.  The groups below sort the headers by how they relate to
that rule.  The comment at the top of each header says what belongs in it and,
where only some code may include it, which code that is.

Headers
-------

Internal to the access methods:

  yb_scan_core.h
  yb_sys_scan_base.h

Extending tableam:

  yb_table_scan_options.h

Execution logic that the planner shares instead of copying:

  yb_scan_plan.h

The YB cost model, mostly planner code that sits under access/ for historical
reasons:

  yb_cost.h

Building pggate requests, used by the access methods and, for now, by some
code above them:

  yb_target.h

Entry points outside the AM interfaces, some of them interim bypasses tracked
in #36168:

  yb_special_scans.h

Bypasses of an AM interface still to be removed, tracked in #36168:

  yb_table_scan.h
  yb_lockrows.h
  yb_parallel_scan.h (the sequential scan side)

Avoid adding a bypass, including a new entry point in one of the headers
above.  When one is unavoidable, declare it in the header of the bypass it
extends or in a new header under src/include/access/ if it is a new kind of
bypass.  That header's comment should name the files that may include it.  It
should also say why no AM interface fits or cite the issue that tracks
removing the bypass.
